tour feature-zoom-graph
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note Two ways to zoom the graph. A trackpad pinch or ctrl+wheel over the canvas zooms around the pointer: the point under the pointer stays under it. The reader reaches for it to shrink a large tree to see its whole shape, or enlarge one area to read it, which 'fit' alone cannot do (TODO.md GUI item 2). The zoom changes in proportion to the gesture (a pinch's magnification, or the wheel's pixel delta, one Zoom step per WHEEL_NOTCH pixels), so a trackpad's many small scroll events add up to the same zoom as one mouse notch of the same distance. The - and + buttons of the zoom cluster in the canvas's bottom-right corner (the map and design-app convention: zoom out, the percentage, zoom in, fit) zoom around the canvas centre to the next of a fixed set of stops (ZOOM_STOPS, 10% to 200%), for a reader with a mouse and no ctrl+wheel habit, or who wants a round zoom back; the percentage between them shows the zoom. Either way the zoom is a font size. It goes down until the graph font is SMALLEST_GRAPH_FONT (a few pixels, an overview where boxes and edges are legible but text is not) or Zoom::SMALLEST, whichever is larger.

